course: dictionary
lesson: 14862
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the sentence tells you which one you need. «Rattler» is a good example: it can mean a snake, a baby's toy, a noisy old car, an old train, or even a great story.
explain: «The rattler coiled under the rock, its tail buzzing.» The clues are coiled, rock and buzzing, so a rattler here is a rattlesnake. Ask yourself: what does the rest of the sentence tell me? Then put your meaning back in the sentence and check it still makes sense.
explain: «The baby shook her rattler and giggled.» The clues are baby and shook, so this rattler is a toy that makes a noise. «The old rattler chugged slowly over the bridge» tells us it is a train, because chugged and bridge fit a train, not a snake or a toy.
fact: A rattler is a noun, and it can have more than one meaning.
fact: In American English, «rattler» often means a rattlesnake: a poisonous snake that shakes the rattle on its tail to warn you.
fact: A rattler can also be something that rattles, like a baby's rattle or a noisy old car.
fact: In old Australian and British slang, «rattler» can mean an old train, especially one that rattles.
fact: «A rattler of a story» means something excellent and very lively.
exercise: «The rattler slid under the rock when we came near.» What is a rattler here? | A tall tree | *A rattlesnake | A train | A baby's toy
exercise: Mia says her grandad's car is a rattler because it clanks and shakes. What does rattler mean here? | A very quiet thing | A snake that lives in the desert | *Something noisy that rattles | A kind of sweet
exercise: «That book was a rattler of a story!» What does rattler mean? | A poisonous snake | A slow, quiet train | *Something excellent and lively | A kind of cake
test: «Watch out for rattlers on the trail, the ranger said.» What does rattlers mean here? | Old trains | *Rattlesnakes | Lively stories | A toy that makes a noise
test: «The old rattler rumbled over the bridge at dawn.» What is the rattler? | A baby's toy | *An old train | A lively story | A snake
exam: Which meaning fits «The rattler coiled in the desert sun, its tail shaking»? | A great story | A train | *A rattlesnake | A noisy old car
